--- b1 medium.en: A letter arrives from social security. It says you were overpaid and it wants the money back. If you do not answer, the agency can start keeping half of every monthly check automatically until the debt is gone. Half. But inside the official rules are four moves that can stop it, shrink it, or erase it. Two of them freeze the deductions the day you use them. has no deadline at all, and by the end, you will know which move fits your letter.
