--- b1 large-v3: A letter arrives from Social Security. It says you were overpaid, and it wants the money back. If you do not answer, the agency can start keeping half of every monthly check, automatically, until the debt is gone. Half. But inside the official rules are four moves that can stop it, shrink it, or erase it. Two of them freeze the deductions the day you use them. One has no deadline at all, and by the end, you will know which move fits your letter.
--- b2 medium.en: This is the money backstory, where we turn official rules into real numbers. If that helps, subscribe now and tap the bell so the next breakdown finds you. Now meet Carol, 66. Her social security check is $2,100 a month. Then comes the envelope. It says she was paid $600 too much every month for 15 months. The total she owes, $9,000.
