--- b3 medium.en: First, what is inside that envelope? The Social Security Administration's own manual says the notice must list the total – what you were paid, what you should have been paid, why the amount was different, and the months involved. It must also tell you three rights – to ask for a reconsideration, to ask for a waiver, and to ask for a different repayment rate. every line. One of them matters more than all the others, and it is about a number of days.
